  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SYR009N NW Syria Acute Crisis Joint Response-Implementation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description promeva:title="Description (English)" promeva:type="104" type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This response (NWSJR) will target, as a priority, IDPs newly displaced due to the increase in conflict and instability in southern Idleb and north Hama since 1st April. This Acute Crisis Mechanism was triggered to respond to the increase in needs of this specific population, and the host communities who have received an influx of these IDPs, with the resulting pressure on already-stretched services. CARE focuses on WASH &amp; Protection, World Vision on WASH &amp; Shelter/NFI, Stichting Vluchteling on Cash, Protection &amp; Health and War Child on MPC/
(Child) Protection.</narrative>
  </description>
